<Routines>
<Routine Name="Logic" Type="RLL">
<RLLContent>
<Rung Number="0" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Copyright © Rockwell Automation, Inc.  All Rights Reserved.
============================================================
T_TtoISO_WkDate:  TIME -- Convert Date/Time to ISO 8601 
Week-Numbered Date (e.g., 2014-01-21 --> 2014-W04-2)
============================================================
Version 1.0-00 Release:  2014-01-21
V1.0-00  2014-01-21:  First release for use with PlantPAx Library 3.0-05.
============================================================
This object converts a Date in common form (Year, Month, Day)
to an ISO-8601 Week Date (like 2014-W04-2, meaning Tuesday
in the fourth week of Week-Numbered Year 2014) for 2014-01-21.

The Week-Numbered Year does not necessarily start on January 1.
It can start from December 29 through January 4.  The first week
of an ISO Week-Numbered Year is the week, beginning with Monday
and ending on Sunday, that contains the first THURSDAY of the
calendar year.  See Wikipedia "ISO Week Date" for more information.

Rungs 0 through 5 of this AOI constitute a derivative work of and use a method which is
 Copyright (c) 2008 by Claus Tondering (claus@tondering.dk)
 under the following license:

COPYRIGHT:  These functions are Copyright (c) 2008 by Claus Tondering (claus@tondering.dk)

LICENSE:  The code is distributed under the Boost Software License, which says:

Boost Software License - Version 1.0 - August 17th, 2003

Permission is hereby granted, free of charge, to any person or organization obtaining a copy of
the software and accompanying documentation covered by this license (the "Software") to use,
reporduce, display, distribute, execute, and transmit the Software, and to prepare DERIVATIVE
WORKS OIF THE SOFTWARE <RA emphasis added>, and to permit third-parties to whom the
Software is furnished to do so, all subject to the following:

The copyright notices in the Software and this entire statement, including the above license grant,
this restriction, and the following disclaimer, must be included in all copies of the Software, in
whole or in part, and all derivative works of the Software, unless such copies or derivative works
are solely in the form of machine-executable object code generated by a source language
processor.

THE SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED "AS IS", WITHOUGH WARRANTY OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS OR
IMPLIED, INCLUDING BUT NOT LIMITE TO THE WARRANTIES OF MERCHANTABILITY, FITNESS FOR 
A PARTICULAR PURPOSE, TITLE AND NON-INFRINGEMENT. IN NO EVENT SHALL THE COPYRIGHT
HOLDERS OR ANYONE DISTRIBUTING THE SOFTWARE BE LIABLE FOR ANY DAMAGES OR OTHER
LIABILITY, WHETHER IN CONTRACT, TORT OR OTHERWISE, ARISING FROM, OUT OF OR IN CONNECTION
WITH THE SOFTWARE OR THE USE OR OTHER DEALINGS IN THE SOFTWARE.
<end of license>

Derived directly from function "week_number" in "calfaq.c" version 1.1, 4 April 2008.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[LEQ(Ref_DT.Mo,2)SUB(Ref_DT.Yr,1,Wrk_a)CPT(Wrk_b,Wrk_a/4-Wrk_a/100+Wrk_a/400)CPT(Wrk_c,(Wrk_a-1)/4-(Wrk_a-1)/100+(Wrk_a-1)/400)SUB(Wrk_b,Wrk_c,Wrk_s)CLR(Wrk_e)CPT(Wrk_h,Ref_DT.Da-1+31*(Ref_DT.Mo-1));]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="1" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[GRT(Ref_DT.Mo,2)MOV(Ref_DT.Yr,Wrk_a)CPT(Wrk_b,Wrk_a/4-Wrk_a/100+Wrk_a/400)CPT(Wrk_c,(Wrk_a-1)/4-(Wrk_a-1)/100+(Wrk_a-1)/400)SUB(Wrk_b,Wrk_c,Wrk_s)ADD(Wrk_s,1,Wrk_e)CPT(Wrk_h,Ref_DT.Da+(153*(Ref_DT.Mo-3)+2)/5+58+Wrk_s);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="2" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[CPT(Wrk_j,(Wrk_a+Wrk_b)MOD 7)CPT(Wrk_d,(Wrk_h+Wrk_j-Wrk_e)MOD 7)CPT(Wrk_n,Wrk_h+3-Wrk_d);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="3" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[LES(Wrk_n,0)CPT(Val_ISOWeek,53-(Wrk_j-Wrk_s)/5)SUB(Ref_DT.Yr,1,Val_ISOYear)JMP(Done);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="4" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[CMP((Wrk_n>(364+Wrk_s)))MOV(1,Val_ISOWeek)ADD(Ref_DT.Yr,1,Val_ISOYear)JMP(Done);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="5" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[CPT(Val_ISOWeek,Wrk_n/7+1)MOV(Ref_DT.Yr,Val_ISOYear);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="6" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
CALCULATE THE DAY OF THE WEEK
============================================================
This version of the day of the week is based on:

http://alcor.concordia.ca/~gpkatch/gdate-algorithm.html

(NOTE:  ALL divisions are INTEGER -- truncated -- divisions!)
F = ( month + 9 ) MOD 12
G = year - ( F / 10 )
Gregorian DayNumber [ D ] = ( 365 * G ) + ( G / 4 ) - ( G / 100 ) + ( G / 400 ) + ( ( ( F * 306 ) + 5 ) / 10 ) + day - 1
DayOfWeek = ( DayNumber + 3 ) MOD 7

Taking the "-1" and the "+3" into account, and using the ISO definition for day (1=Monday .. 7=Sunday) gives this:]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[LBL(Done)CPT(Wrk_F,(Ref_DT.Mo+9)MOD 12)CPT(Wrk_G,Ref_DT.Yr-(Wrk_F/10))CPT(Val_ISODay,((365*Wrk_G+(Wrk_G/4)-(Wrk_G/100)+(Wrk_G/400)+((Wrk_F*306+5)/10)+Ref_DT.Da+1)MOD 7)+1);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="7" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Calculate the day of the week for Jan 1 this year.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[MOV(10,Wrk_F)SUB(Val_ISOYear,1,Wrk_G)CPT(Wrk_Jan1DoW,((365*Wrk_G+(Wrk_G/4)-(Wrk_G/100)+(Wrk_G/400)+((Wrk_F*306+5)/10)+2)MOD 7)+1);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="8" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Calculate the day of the week for Dec 1 this year.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[MOV(9,Wrk_F)MOV(Val_ISOYear,Wrk_G)CPT(Wrk_Dec31DoW,((365*Wrk_G+(Wrk_G/4)-(Wrk_G/100)+(Wrk_G/400)+((Wrk_F*306+5)/10)+32)MOD 7)+1);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="9" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If either day falls on a Thursday, this ISO Year has 53 weeks.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[EQU(Wrk_Jan1DoW,4) ,EQU(Wrk_Dec31DoW,4) ]MOV(53,Val_WeeksInISOYear);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="10" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If neither day falls on a Thursday, this ISO Year has 52 weeks.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[NEQ(Wrk_Jan1DoW,4)NEQ(Wrk_Dec31DoW,4)MOV(52,Val_WeeksInISOYear);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
</RLLContent>
</Routine>
</Routines>
<Dependencies>
<Dependency Type="DataType" Name="DateTime"/>
</Dependencies>
</AddOnInstructionDefinition>
</AddOnInstructionDefinitions>
</Controller>
